id: pm-qudvto
title: "Terminal relationship backfill, evidence-derived tranche: make every closed and canceled item reachable by typed graph traversal"
description: "Terminal items were the tracker's largest blind spot: of 1,795 closed and canceled items, 1,024 had no outbound relationship edge at all, 822 had none in either direction, and 1,682 had no edge of any kind that semantic traversal accepts. Since predecessors, ancestors and successors reject related-kind edges, and the scalar parent field is not itself a traversable semantic kind, the entire completed history of the project was invisible to graph algorithms even where hierarchy existed. This tranche closes that gap for every terminal item reachable from durable evidence, in one changelog-safe pass made possible by the release attribution stamp landed in the same lane.\n\nFour evidence classes, applied in order of strength, none of them inferential:\n\n1. Typed hierarchy mirror. Every terminal item carrying a parent gains a typed implements edge to that parent, so the lineage that already existed as a scalar becomes traversable. This is the same mechanism that made active items reach their outcome milestones.\n\n2. Explicit identifier references. Every pm identifier recorded in an item's own durable text — description, body, comments, notes, resolution, close reason, acceptance criteria — becomes a related edge to that item, provided the target exists and the edge is not already present. These are references the authoring agent or human wrote deliberately.\n\n3. Shared linked artifact. Items still edgeless after the first two classes link to the items with which they share the most linked files or docs, since two items acting on the same artifact are related by subject.\n\n4. Shared issue reference. Items still edgeless after the first three link to items citing the same GitHub issue or pull request number.\n\nItems that remain unlinked after all four classes are recorded as a residual rather than given fabricated edges, per the parent item's requirement that unresolved cases retain uncertainty."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:graph",backfill,changelog-safe,context-management,history,relationships,terminal-items
created_at: "2026-07-26T17:15:45.262Z"
