claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#ad0de54baae9cc12afd5a5a6"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Every edge added cites one of the four declared evidence classes, and no edge is created from title similarity, release cohort, or any other inferential signal; Edges are deduplicated against what already exists in either direction so the pass is idempotent and safe to re-run; Each write is an ordinary history-recorded mutation carrying the evidence class in its message, so the enrichment is itself auditable; Items with no evidence in any class are recorded as a residual with counts, not given fabricated links; Changelog regeneration after the pass shows no bucket movement, proving the release stamp made the write attribution-neutral; Graph audit reports no new cycles and no new findings after the pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Turn the completed history of the project into a graph that algorithms can walk, without inventing a single edge"
value: "Closed work becomes first-class institutional context for precedent retrieval, release archaeology and long-horizon planning"
impact: "Removes the tracker's largest structural blind spot: the majority of its own items were previously unreachable by typed traversal"
outcome: "Every terminal item with durable evidence carries typed relationship edges, with a recorded residual for those that have none"
why_now: "Release attribution is now stamped, so metadata writes on closed items are changelog-neutral and the pass can finally run"
parent: pm-lnrk
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Applied 3,744 evidence-derived relationship edges across 1,713 terminal items using four declared evidence classes, making the completed history of the project traversable by typed graph algorithms without inventing a single link."
expected_result: "Every terminal item with durable evidence carries typed relationship edges, the pass introduces no cycles or validation findings, and changelog attribution is unaffected because release identifiers are stamped."
actual_result: "1,713 items updated with zero failures; edges 5,147 to 8,891 (implements 317 to 1,932, related 2,260 to 4,360); graph audit reports the identical 11 pre-existing info findings with identical affected-subject counts; validate ok with only the legacy resolution warning at 289; health ok with zero warnings; changelog shows 0 release-section moves, 0 category moves and identical byte count across the pass."
