close_reason: "Delivered and verified. Evidence-derived relationship edges applied across 1,713 terminal items using four declared classes and no inferential signal: typed hierarchy mirror to an existing parent, explicit pm identifiers recorded in the item's own durable text, shared linked file or doc, and shared GitHub issue or pull request reference. Every write is an ordinary history-recorded mutation carrying its evidence class in the message, deduplicated against existing edges in both directions so the pass is idempotent. Items with no evidence in any class were recorded as a residual rather than given fabricated links. Reachability is demonstrated rather than asserted: a previously edgeless closed item now reaches 1,444 nodes through semantic traversal.\n\nChangelog neutrality proved at scale, which was the acceptance criterion this tranche existed to satisfy: 3,744 edge writes across 1,713 closed items produced 0 release-section moves, 0 category moves, 0 items added or removed, and an identical 296,429-byte output. Rows did reorder inside the sections they never left, which is a separate residual now owned by pm-nwuzaq. Graph audit after the pass reports the same 11 findings, the same four codes and the same affected-subject counts as before, so no cycle and no new finding was introduced; validate stays ok with only the pre-existing legacy resolution warning at 289, and health reports ok with zero warnings. Edge totals moved from 5,147 to 8,891, with implements 317 to 1,932 and related 2,260 to 4,360."
